      "description": "A flat white area for a question, answer, or progress task.",
      "html": "<section class=\"ds-work-panel\"><h2>Your answer</h2><p>Choose an answer, then lock it in.</p></section>",
      "css": ".ds-work-panel{font-family:'Manrope Variable',sans-serif;background:#fff;border:1px solid var(--line,#dde0ea);border-radius:12px;padding:30px;min-width:0;color:var(--ink,#29264b)}.ds-work-panel h2{margin:0;font-size:18px;font-weight:740;line-height:1.35;letter-spacing:-.02em}.ds-work-panel p{font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;color:var(--muted,#685d75);margin:12px 0 0;max-width:72ch}@media(max-width:1150px){.ds-work-panel{padding:24px}}@media(max-width:650px){.ds-work-panel{padding:24px 22px}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Selected Format",
      "kind": "button",
      "refersTo": "format-option",
      "description": "An option tile selected with a border, pale fill, and check cue.",
      "html": "<button type=\"button\" class=\"ds-format ds-format-selected\" aria-pressed=\"true\"><span class=\"ds-format-icons\"><svg width=\"18\" height=\"18\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m3 5 2 2 4-4M13 6h8M13 12h8M13 18h8m-18-1 2 2 4-4\"/></svg><svg width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m20 6-11 11-5-5\"/></svg></span><strong>Quiz</strong><small>Choose the right answer</small></button>",
      "css": ".ds-format{font-family:'Manrope Variable',sans-serif;background:#fff;border:1px solid #d4d7e2;padding:15px 14px;text-align:left;border-radius:7px;min-width:0;color:var(--ink,#29264b);line-height:1.5;cursor:pointer}.ds-format-selected{border:2px solid var(--accent,#6b54ad);padding:14px 13px;background:#f5f1fc}.ds-format-icons{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;color:var(--accent,#6b54ad);margin-bottom:12px;gap:48px}.ds-format strong{font-size:14px;display:block;font-weight:700}.ds-format small{font-size:10px;color:var(--muted,#685d75);display:block;margin-top:4px}.ds-format:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--focus,#a48bce);outline-offset:4px;}.ds-format:disabled{opacity:.48;cursor:not-allowed}@media(max-width:650px){.ds-format{padding:13px 11px}.ds-format-selected{padding:12px 10px}.ds-format strong{font-size:13px}.ds-format small{font-size:9px;line-height:1.5;margin-top:5px}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Paired Round Progress",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "round-mark",
      "description": "Aligned positions show each player’s current round and outcomes.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-progress\"><div class=\"ds-progress-row\"><span>You</span><div><span class=\"ds-round ds-round-correct\" aria-label=\"Round 1 correct\"><svg width=\"12\" height=\"12\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m20 6-11 11-5-5\"/></svg></span><span class=\"ds-round ds-round-current\" aria-label=\"Round 2 current\">2</span><span class=\"ds-round\">3</span><span class=\"ds-round\">4</span></div></div><div class=\"ds-progress-row ds-progress-other\"><span>Alex</span><div><span class=\"ds-round ds-round-incorrect\" aria-label=\"Round 1 incorrect\"><svg width=\"12\" height=\"12\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m18 6-12 12M6 6l12 12\"/></svg></span><span class=\"ds-round ds-round-current\" aria-label=\"Round 2 current\">2</span><span class=\"ds-round\">3</span><span class=\"ds-round\">4</span></div></div></div>",
      "css": ".ds-progress{font-family:'Manrope Variable',sans-serif;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:5px;margin:17px 3px 29px}.ds-progress-row{display:flex;gap:15px;align-items:center}.ds-progress-row>span{font-size:10px;width:90px;color:var(--muted,#685d75);overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;white-space:nowrap}.ds-progress-row>div{display:flex;gap:5px;flex:1;min-width:0}.ds-round{flex:1;max-width:64px;height:19px;border-radius:4px;background:#e8e5ef;color:var(--muted,#685d75);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-size:9px;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.ds-round-current{background:#dad0ef;color:#654a9c;border:1px solid #aa95d0}.ds-round-correct{background:#d9ece5;color:var(--success,#267465)}.ds-round-incorrect{background:#efdedf;color:var(--danger,#9a4555)}.ds-progress-other .ds-round-current{background:#f0e1ca;border-color:#cfb288;color:#805921}@media(max-width:650px){.ds-progress{margin:15px 0 23px}.ds-progress-row{gap:8px}.ds-progress-row>span{width:48px;font-size:9px}.ds-progress-row>div{gap:3px}.ds-round{height:16px;font-size:8px}.ds-round>svg{width:10px}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Java Editor Shell",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "editor",
      "description": "The light file-tab and code typography; the app uses CodeMirror for editing.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-editor\"><div class=\"ds-editor-tab\"><svg width=\"15\" height=\"15\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m18 16 4-4-4-4M6 8l-4 4 4 4m12-9-4 18\"/></svg>Main.java<span>Java</span></div><textarea class=\"ds-code\" aria-label=\"Java code editor preview\" spellcheck=\"false\">public class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        System.out.println(42);\n    }\n}</textarea></div>",
      "css": ".ds-editor{font-family:'Manrope Variable',sans-serif;border:1px solid #ddd7e6;border-radius:7px;overflow:hidden;max-width:100%;color:var(--ink,#29264b);background:#fff}.ds-editor-tab{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:7px;padding:11px 13px;background:#f4f1f8;border-bottom:1px solid #e1dbe8;font-size:11px;line-height:1.5}.ds-editor-tab span{margin-left:auto;color:var(--muted,#685d75);font-size:10px}.ds-code{display:block;width:100%;height:310px;border:0;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Consolas,monospace;font-size:12px;text-align:left;background:#fff;color:var(--ink,#29264b);white-space:pre;resize:none;caret-color:var(--accent,#6b54ad)}.ds-code:focus{outline:2px solid var(--focus,#a48bce);outline-offset:-2px}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Campus scorebook",
    "overview": "A clear university score sheet gives shared study a friendly competitive rhythm. Cool paper, white work areas, and a dark plum navigation bar hold the interface together. Violet identifies the player's actions; warm ochre distinguishes the opponent. The light appearance is the user-selected visual identity.\n\nThe atmosphere is composed, approachable, and focused on reading. Strong sentence-case headings sit above compact labels and generous work areas. Paired scores and round marks make the contest visible while questions, formulas, and code remain the main work. Imagery is code-native: Lucide SVG icons, mathematical notation, and a simple SVG rating chart.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Cool light ground with flat white work panels.",
      "Self-hosted Manrope for headings, controls, and prose.",
      "Violet player actions and ochre opponent identity.",
      "Paired scores and aligned strips of round outcomes.",
      "Restrained borders, moderate corners, and quiet state changes."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Color Has a Job Rule",
        "body": "Use violet for the player's actions and selections, ochre for the opposing player, and success or error colors for outcomes with a written or icon cue.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Stable Numbers Rule",
        "body": "Use tabular numerals for changing scores, clocks, ratings, and comparable numeric answers so columns and digit widths stay steady.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat Work Surface Rule",
        "body": "Keep ordinary cards and answer panels flat; reserve shadows for transient overlays.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** keep the user-selected light ground, white work panels, and plum navigation across new surfaces.",
      "**Do** use self-hosted Manrope, sentence-case labels, and tabular numerals for scores and clocks.",
      "**Do** preserve written or icon cues beside meaningful status colors.",
      "**Do** keep both players' round positions aligned and the active timer visible on phones.",
      "**Do** use local scrolling for long code, formulas, and tables while the page fits its viewport.",
      "**Do** retain visible keyboard focus and honor reduced-motion preferences."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** substitute the earlier sketch's color values for the implemented tokens.",
      "**Don't** add decorative photography or illustration to this code-native study world.",
      "**Don't** add shadows to ordinary work panels or nest shadowed cards inside them.",
      "**Don't** turn score, rating, and time numerals into proportional-width text.",
      "**Don't** use a system display face or text glyphs in place of the shipped Manrope and SVG icon vocabulary."
    ]
  }
}
